  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920. Counted 16 January 1920 by the returning officer, T. M. Wilson (town clerk). The ward returned 4 members. M'Nally (137) took the last seat over Poots (127) on the sixth count, short of the quota. The results sheets give surnames only; first names are from the Northern Whig's list of the elected. Candidates with no party label were not on the official Unionist list and no report seen gives their party."
